 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "While Chef Barinov laments that his lifelong dream of a Michelin star is ruined, Fedya returns and proudly announces that he locked the inspector inside the walk-in refrigerator so he wouldn't cause problems.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Прошу вас, здесь совсем недалеко.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вы сломали мечту моей жизни.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Какой отчёт он сейчас напишет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Виктор Петрович, может всё обойдётся?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы потом вкусно его накормим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Назови мне хоть одну причину.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я запер его в холодильнике.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Зачем ты это сейчас сделал?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вы же сами мне намекали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Если отпустим, он создаст проблемы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А сейчас он не создаст?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сейчас мы что-нибудь придумаем, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Прошу вас, здесь совсем недалеко.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'After you, it is very close by.' Fedya brings out the contrast between 'ask for' and 'you' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вы сломали мечту моей жизни.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You broke the dream of my life.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'you', while 'life' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Какой отчёт он сейчас напишет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What kind of report will he write now?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'what' and finishing on 'will write'. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Виктор Петрович, может всё обойдётся?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Viktor Petrovich, maybe it will blow over?' Senya anchors the line on 'maybe', while 'will do' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы потом вкусно его накормим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will feed him deliciously later.' In Russian, the idea of 'we' flows naturally into 'will feed' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Назови мне хоть одну причину.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Name me at least one reason.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'name' and finishing on 'an excuse'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я запер его в холодильнике.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I locked him in the refrigerator.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'fridge' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Зачем ты это сейчас сделал?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why did you do that just now?' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'why', while 'made' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вы же сами мне намекали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You hinted at it to me yourself.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'to hint' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Если отпустим, он создаст проблемы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If we let him go, he will create problems.' Fedya anchors the line on 'if', while 'problems' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А сейчас он не создаст?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And right now he will not create any?' In spoken Russian, the words stay in their normal statement order and Chef Barinov's rising voice at the end turns the line into a question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сейчас мы что-нибудь придумаем, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now we will think of something, Chef.' The meaning hinges on 'now' working together with 'to think up' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
